WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.840
1 of 6. First, interview the stakeholder
Open Stakeholder interview. Ask Dana about the overdue report and clarify the topics in Interview evidence before you write your story.

2
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:14.760
2 of 6. Use the brief and interview evidence
Show brief opens the case file. Its Brief explains the task; Interview evidence keeps the topics settled by the conversation. Use what you learn to decide what the report must do.

3
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.680
3 of 6. Next, shape your backlog
Open My backlog to read the supplied stories and create or edit US-4. Write the story and acceptance criteria in its form, then choose Save story and check the save status.

4
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:27.320
4 of 6. Check your saved story
In My backlog, choose Check the story to inspect its structure. Resolve missing fields before you ask for a review. A structural check does not pass the phase.

5
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:34.120
5 of 6. Submit, read feedback, revise
Submit for review sends the saved story. Open the backlog’s Review view for its actual feedback. Revise the story and resubmit when needed; only a recorded passing review opens the next phase.

6
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:40.200
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
